WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.000
E-mail, one of the most widespread digital communications services.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.000
We use it every day...

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.000
at work...

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.000
to talk to friends...

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.500
to communicate with our bank...

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.500
or to shop online.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Email providers enable email communication between sender and recipient.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.500
But... are your email communications protected?

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.500
If your email communication is not properly secured,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.500
attackers can easily open and read your messages,

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.000
change the content,

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:41.000
add dangerous attachments, or even send fraudulent messages in your name.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.500
In order to check whether your email provider offers a good level of protection in your email communications,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.000
at the Joint Research Centre of the European Commission we have developed the MECSA research project.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.000
Simply submit your email address and reply to the email you will receive.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.500
You will immediately receive your results, informing you about how your email provider scored considering three significant categories.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.000
to see if the privacy of your email communications is ensured.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.000
to confirm that you are protected from identity theft

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.000
to show if your email content is at risk of being modified

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.000
By participating in the MECSA research project,

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:37.000
you finally have the means to check the level of protection of email communications that your email provider is offering you.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.500
By using MECSA, you can help us with our research on the security of email communications...

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.000
and contribute to improving the overall security level of the email ecosystem.

